From bb81eecaee1b265931418fe2ec195e67058caf88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:12:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve compiler preprocessing policy in hermetic bindgen

Retain optimization and warning options alongside their paired arguments when adapting the compiler command for bindgen. Translate MSVC warning-error switches to Clang driver syntax and retain the existing deterministic macro-redaction policy. Expose the filtering boundary for focused tests and include its suite in the repository Bazel checks.

TDD: the original filter fails two focused outcome assertions for missing optimization and warning flags and discarded MSVC /WX (bazel-red.log, exit 3). All six regressions pass after repair (bazel-green.log, exit 0). Actual AWS-LC binding generation runs without the previous macro or fortify warnings (aws-lc-bindings.log, exit 0). A deliberate header warning fails binding generation at expected_bindgen_warning (warning-negative.log, exit 1). just fmt-check passes (format-final.log); emitted checks are recorded separately.

Base: rust-v0.162.1, 092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d. Refs holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#61.
